{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478385-specific-question-about-masks-terra-incognitae","id":1478385,"title":"Specific question about \"Masks\" Terra Incognitae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-09T09:49:23-07:00","id":1478385,"title":"Specific question about \"Masks\" Terra Incognitae","content":"Hello again,<br /> <br /> I know &quot;Masks of the Mythos&quot; isn't out yet, but I'm curious about the Terra Incognitae that are in the manuscript. I'm thinking about adapting some of the locations that I know of for a product of my own, but I don't want to double-dip.<br /> <br /> Are there any IRL locations in Rhode Island that made it in? If so, which ones? (I'm most interested in HP Lovecraft's actual residence, and/or &quot;<a href=\"http://www.historyshomes.com/detail.cfm?id=362\" target=\"_blank\">The Shunned House</a>,&quot; which was based on another IRL location)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","name":"brokenimage321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T10:42:55-07:00","id":1478391,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to check, but I don\u2019t recall as much on literal terra incognita as on the Miskatonic River Valley in Massachusetts (where Arkham, Innsmoth, Kingsport, etc are) as a fully fleshed out setting.<br /> <br /> That said I\u2019m sure there was word count to Ry\u2019leth, and buried locals of less human seeming civilizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T18:09:31-07:00","id":1478452,"title":"","content":"Not seeing anything specific for Rhode Island in the manuscript or on the Lovecraft wiki. I do see a reference in passing To the 'Halsey House' in the section for The Case of Charles Dexter Ward. <a href=\"https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/The_Case_of_Charles_Dexter_Ward\" target=\"_blank\">https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Th...es_Dexter_Ward</a> on the wiki. I've been quietly using Doggerland in the Northern European areas to have weird artifacts that have come to Innsmouth, and Arkham for research. Providence does not appear to have Terra Incognita per se, but it is associated with at least several incidents that I would think something might show up eventually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","user":"TheWanderingJewels","date":". 04-09-2022, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}